# Conventional Commits offer

When you change files in the workspace (create, edit, delete, rename), end the turn by **offering** a commit subject (and optional body) in [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) form.

## Format

```text
<type>(<optional scope>): <short description>
```

Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`.

- Imperative mood, lowercase description, no trailing period
- Keep the subject ~72 characters or less
- Scope is optional (e.g. `benchmark`, `harness`, `metrics`)
- Offer only — do **not** create a git commit unless the user explicitly asks

## Example offers

```text
feat(benchmark): add smoke gate for skill arms
```

```text
fix(structure): exclude graphify-out from LOC metrics
```
